# Copy to .env.local (never committed). Leave ZS_API_URL empty to run on the in-memory
# demo data for Halden & Rowe Fine Jewelry, with no sign-in.
#
# Every value is server-only. The browser calls the dashboard's own /api proxy, which sends
# the signed-in person's own Supabase access token on the server; nothing here is inlined
# into page JS (the build checks). Set ZS_API_URL for `build` (it decides demo or live mode)
# and everything for `start` or `dev`.
ZS_API_URL=

# Supabase Auth (live mode only). People sign in with an email link; the session lives in
# httpOnly cookies on this server. Live mode answers 503 while either value is missing.
# The project URL, e.g. https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL=
# The project's anon (publishable) key. Kept on the server: the browser never talks to Supabase.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# In the Supabase project:
# - Auth > URL Configuration: Site URL and the only redirect URL are this dashboard's
#   https origin plus /auth/confirm (e.g. https://app.example.com/auth/confirm**).
# - Auth > Email Templates > Magic Link: link to
#   {{ .RedirectTo }}&token_hash={{ .TokenHash }}&type=email
#   so the link works on any device (no PKCE verifier needed).
# - Disable sign-ups: people join only by invitation (the dashboard never creates users).

# Sign-in link requests per 15 minutes: per address (1-10000, default 5) and in total
# (1-10000, default 30). They count in the API's shared Postgres limiter, so they hold across
# server instances.
DASHBOARD_SIGN_IN_PER_ADDRESS=
DASHBOARD_SIGN_IN_GLOBAL=
# Required for sign-in: trimmed, 32+ characters, no whitespace, the same value as
# SIGN_IN_LIMITER_SECRET on the API project. Deploy the API with its secret first. Without a
# valid value (or with a ZS_API_URL that is not https, or http beyond localhost) no sign-in
# link is sent (502) and the server log says why, once.
DASHBOARD_SIGN_IN_LIMITER_SECRET=
# Set to 1 only behind a reverse proxy that sets X-Forwarded-Host, -Proto and -For. Then the
# origin check uses X-Forwarded-Host, the cookies are Secure when X-Forwarded-Proto is https,
# and sign-in rate limits key on the address the proxy appended to X-Forwarded-For (its
# right-most entry). Leave empty otherwise: then all callers share one sign-in limit.
DASHBOARD_TRUST_PROXY=
